{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9785-building-an-embed","id":9785,"title":"Building an Embed.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-13T09:56:49-08:00","id":9785,"title":"Building an Embed.","content":"Over on the RPG.net forums long before Demon came out, I was talking about building a custom Embed to teleport via doorways, drawing from the Keymaker from <i>The Matrix: Reloaded </i>and (at the advice of BlackHat_Matt) <i>The Adjustment Bureau</i>. It was suggested as <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?680110-Demon-The-Descent-What-Do-You-Want-From-It-Part-II&amp;p=16891402#post16891402\" target=\"_blank\">totally</a> and completely <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?680110-Demon-The-Descent-What-Do-You-Want-From-It-Part-II&amp;p=16860592#post16860592\" target=\"_blank\">doable</a>. Now that we've got the Demon rules available, I'm taking a shot at the crunch. Here's what I have so far:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Backdoor</b>, Mundane Embed.<br /> <br /> Using utility corridors put in place by the God-Machine, the Demon can exploit the conceptual nature of doorways to connect two distant locations.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits + [Stealth, Larceny, Streetwise, Investigation??]<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>The Demon opens a doorway, connecting it to another within Primum miles they can clearly picture and have visited before. This always triggers a Compromise roll.</div> <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:06:09-08:00","id":9793,"title":"","content":"I'd give it an Aether costs and make it an Exploit, but it seems radical to me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:11:42-08:00","id":9798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metrophelean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9785-building-an-embed?p=9793#post9793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd give it an Aether costs and make it an Exploit, but it seems radical to me!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I kind of felt the same, but made it an Embed given the advice I linked to in the post, which suggested it would fit well as an Embed, especially as one valid as prerequisite to (what I believe to be) Rip the Gates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:14:55-08:00","id":9799,"title":"","content":"Hrm. I'd likely tone down the distance, then. Maybe it has to be linked to a place you visited in a previous scene? Or <i>the</i> previous scene?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:19:53-08:00","id":9801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metrophelean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9785-building-an-embed?p=9799#post9799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it has to be linked to a place you visited in a previous scene?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it does have to be a place you've been before. That's already there. I could see a restriction of having to have been there in the past day or week, maybe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:25:44-08:00","id":9808,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Primum in miles does seem extreme...but only in cities. Using this Embed in a rural area, you might not be able to get anywhere even within a couple of miles. <br /> <br /> I'd remove the mandatory compromise (it's an Embed) and stipulate that multiple uses over a short period of time <i>can</i> trigger a compromise, plus angels use these back pathways, too, and you never know when you'll see one. The distance thing, I'd need to noodle a bit more, but maybe it's not tied to distance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:28:10-08:00","id":9810,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Primum miles was just the only idea I had. <i>Perfectly </i>willing to either reduce that or do some else entirely. Maybe... the character can designate [Primum] doors that are tied to the power? You can travel to those and no others?<br /> <br /> Edit: Would need to add a bit saying if you can change the doors on this list, how that is done (maybe touch it and spend a point of Willpower?) and maybe a limit on how often you can do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":478,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","user":"Intrepid Vector","date":". 11-13-2013, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:30:23-08:00","id":9811,"title":"","content":"Ooh, that's kind of cool. I'd be inclined to let you have 1 door/Primum dot, but let you &quot;untether&quot; doors and attune new ones as necessary, maybe with an Aether expenditure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:43:24-08:00","id":9824,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:9px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Woo, think we've arrived at something very neat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Should the Demon be able to bring others through with them as long as the doorway stays open?</span><br /> <br /> (I am making this one of my starting embeds and no one is allowed to stop me)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:45:24-08:00","id":9828,"title":"","content":"Maybe something like this: &quot;The Demon can designate up to [Primum+1] doors to connect in this manner, in-between which he and <b>anyone else with this Embed</b> may travel freely. A door may be designated with a simple touch, and remains part of the Demon's network indefinitely until released (either deliberately or through the demon's demise). Both Demons and Angels have to be careful with this power, as it's possible for an enterprising agent of the other side to infiltrate and even co-opt gateways. Stealing a door from another network invokes a Clash of Wills between the Demon and the current 'owner'.&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Now I'm seeing an Interlock built around this and In My Pocket that lets a Demon create an extra-dimensional labyrinth, accessible through linked doorways. Perhaps including something like Cuckoo's Egg or The Map is Not the Territory to swap around rooms and make it into a Cube like prison box. Then lure Angels inside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-13-2013, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:53:07-08:00","id":9833,"title":"","content":"The Clash of Wills seems a little unnecessary and your version seems to say that you can only travel BETWEEN designated doors, instead of TO a designated door from any normal door? Which makes this power useless at Primum 1 if that's your intention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:59:35-08:00","id":9839,"title":"","content":"Oop, good note about the number of doors. Primum + 1 it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T11:28:23-08:00","id":9865,"title":"","content":"I have to say, it makes me inordinately happy to see people talking about Interlocks. Or really, these powers at all. Makes my work see worthwhile. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T11:51:22-08:00","id":9878,"title":"","content":"This was exactly the power that I wanted as soon as I heard what demon was about (largely thanks to The Adjustment Bureau). The original system you proposed is actually very similar to the fifth dot of the directional court contract for changelings, though I don't know if that makes it sound more or less balanced (I feel like balance with demon is going to get really weird in general). Still, I'm loving both versions of the idea and I'm really hoping that if I end up playing demon I can use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T15:59:39-08:00","id":10052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9785-building-an-embed?p=9865#post9865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, it makes me inordinately happy to see people talking about Interlocks. Or really, these powers at all. Makes my work see worthwhile. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well I love your work, Matt <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I think my favorite powers have to be Never Here and Four Minutes ago. Avoidance Kata for everyone, hehehe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T19:33:27-08:00","id":10135,"title":"","content":"I just remembered I never worked out what Skill to use with this power, as shown above. Does anyone have a suggestion of which of the possible skills I listed would be most appropriate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T21:15:55-08:00","id":10184,"title":"","content":"I need help creating a power; almost certainly an Exploit.<br /> <br /> I need something that can summon Angels, either as a &quot;false Demon&quot; beacon or the ability to blow someone else's Cover/stick them with the Hunted condition. Any help?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T03:13:50-08:00","id":10290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intrepid Vector</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9785-building-an-embed?p=10135#post10135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just remembered I never worked out what Skill to use with this power, as shown above. Does anyone have a suggestion of which of the possible skills I listed would be most appropriate?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's something specifically meant to be urban, I'd go with Streetwise. Just like knowing a shortcut through alleys, y'know? Just a better one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T04:42:00-08:00","id":10327,"title":"","content":"I don't know, I like the implication of using Larceny as the Skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T06:41:37-08:00","id":10361,"title":"","content":"My favorite power is probably Play on Words, but it was a gift for my wife. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T06:55:37-08:00","id":10372,"title":"","content":"Oh yes, it has a certain appeal, for surrealism if nothing else, but I'm more the type to groan at a pun than smile, haha. Common Misconception's another fun one, I feel, especially if the player roleplays the 'fact' the Demon gives.<br /> <br /> Do you have anything you might be able to contribute regarding the question of what Skill to use for the Backdoor Embed, Matt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T07:25:00-08:00","id":10388,"title":"","content":"What class of Embed is Backdoor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T07:46:06-08:00","id":10404,"title":"","content":"Mundane. Something to flit from place to place like this seemed very Wheels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T08:06:06-08:00","id":10411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intrepid Vector</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9785-building-an-embed?p=10372#post10372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yes, it has a certain appeal, for surrealism if nothing else, but I'm more the type to groan at a pun than smile, haha. Common Misconception's another fun one, I feel, especially if the player roleplays the 'fact' the Demon gives.<br /> <br /> Do you have anything you might be able to contribute regarding the question of what Skill to use for the Backdoor Embed, Matt?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're calling it Backdoor, huh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm 12, apparently. <br /> <br /> Anyway, Skill. Hrm. Streetwise would be my first thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T08:20:45-08:00","id":10422,"title":"","content":"Haha, well it was Backdoor or Shortcut and I just picked one. I don't read innuendos into things as readily as most people, haha. I might change it to the latter.<br /> <br /> Thanks for weighing in. All the <i>more </i>reason for my Fixer/social character to know people* :P<br /> <br /> <br /> As a completely unrelated thing, I seem to have made my Demon REALLY hard to pin down and kill, unless he gets overwhelmed or trapped. Invisibility, line of sight teleportation, this door teleportation, and retconning himself out of a scene, taken together, are pretty potent not-dying, not-being-here powers. Plus later a Bolthole with Easy Access and Trap Door so, man, if he escapes out of sight he's pretty much gone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*I have spliced together Sam from Burn Notice with the Keymaker from the Matrix. TELL NO ONE.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":478,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","user":"Intrepid Vector","date":". 11-14-2013, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T09:56:26-08:00","id":10513,"title":"","content":"That's awesome. That means if he ever risks getting pinned down, it's because he's choosing to make himself vulnerable. I like those stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T03:34:12-08:00","id":11148,"title":"","content":"Backdoor and Shortcut both have computing associations, which seems to be a bit of a theme in Demon. Backdoor makes it more hacker, Shortcut more general use, IMO - so I'd call it Backdoor if you expect to be using it for DARING HEISTS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T12:23:58-08:00","id":13542,"title":"","content":"Backdoor makes more sense than Shortcut if we're going the computing route, since a Backdoor is a little bit of exploitable weakness or entry into something that the programmers (God-Machine and its Angels) know about, but that someone else (Demons) would have to discover. At least, that's my understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T14:54:10-08:00","id":13631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9785-building-an-embed?p=13542#post13542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Backdoor makes more sense than Shortcut if we're going the computing route, since a Backdoor is a little bit of exploitable weakness or entry into something that the programmers (God-Machine and its Angels) know about, but that someone else (Demons) would have to discover. At least, that's my understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whereas a Shortcut is just &quot;well I use this thing a lot so I have a method for getting there extra fast,&quot; which is kind of the effect of the Embed, even if it does it by using backdoors in the universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T15:00:51-08:00","id":13639,"title":"","content":"So it's a Shortcut that is a Backdoor. XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T23:24:58-07:00","id":175807,"title":"","content":"Little bit of a necro, but I remembered this thread while thinking about Demon, and how much I like this idea for an Embed. So I took a crack at it.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I used the Primum Miles version of the idea and wrote up a version of the Embed. Let me know what you guys think.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Backdoor</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A door is a portal between two different spaces. Demons who learn the Backdoor Embed learn how to exploit this conceptual relationship and the uncertainty that is inherent in any closed door. Any random door could lead </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">anywhere</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">. Humans may </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">think </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">a door will lead them where they want to go, but a Demon can </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">make </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">it so.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">First, the door in question must be closed and must not have been opened in the same scene that this Embed is used. Second, the destination must be one that the Demon can clearly visualize. Many Demons target supply closets and other infrequently used doors with Backdoor, and it is used for infiltration as often as for escape.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Wits + Streetwise</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Action:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Instant</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Roll Results</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dramatic Failure:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> The demon\u2019s door not only fails to lead them to their desired destination, it spits them out of a random door within Primum miles of their point of entry, disoriented. The demon suffers the Stunned Tilt upon arrival. Additionally, witnessing their sudden appearance through the door will likely prompt compromise.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Failure:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> The demon fails to connect the two portals. Opening the door leads to its usually intended destination. Additionally, that door cannot be used to activate Backdoor for the rest of the scene.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Success:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> The demon successfully connects the two portals, allowing access to a nearby door that\u2019s within Primum miles. The two doors are connected for one additional turn per success. This effect can be reflexively cancelled by the demon, severing the connection if attempting a quick getaway.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Exceptional Success:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> The connection between the two portals lasts until the end of the scene, and can be cancelled reflexively by the demon. Additionally, they can sense anyone who steps through either end of the Backdoor.</span></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think I have one concern about my Dramatic Failure. I think it's a really cool last resort option. Let's say you're running from the cops and you approach a supply closet and try to use Backdoor to escape. You fail your roll, just your luck. Either you can sit on your failure and figure out some other way of escaping, or you can opt for that dramatic failure. Then Backdoor works! Only... it puts you at some random door within a mile. The possibilities are endless in a city, and many of them could be bad for your health. One guy might wind up in the sewers and make his getaway. Another might wind up at open elevator doors when the elevator hasn't arrived yet, etc.<br /> <br /> That randomness could be a hook for more craziness. Is it too weird or inappropriate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":".  Cleaned up the description a bit. 06-21-2014, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T03:33:24-07:00","id":175904,"title":"","content":"I really liked Leetsepeak's dramatic failure condition on his rendition of the embed. I decided to have a go at my own version of this embed, please let me know what you think!<br /> <br /> <b>Employee Access</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">A doorway is a portal, the terms are synonymous with one another. Demons understand this reality on a level beyond the limited human concept, realising that a door has the potential to go anywhere. The God-Machine often uses the potentiality of doors to deploy its angels, it does this via a \u201clocation\u201d known as \u201cthe hallway\u201d. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">A demon with this embed has potential access to the Hallway. The demon can choose a door that has not been opened during the scene and activate this embed; when he does the demon must elect to open the door to the Hallway</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"> or to a destination doorway that he can visualise clearly (such as a place he has been or seen), if he is already within the Hallway.</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"> The door the demon used to access the Hallway will continue to access it until it is closed or until the scene ends. Once inside the Hallway the demon must use this embed a second time in order to get a door that enters his desired location. This embed does not unlock the destination door. <i>Note: He does not </i><i><b>have</b></i><i> to use this embed to leave the Hallway, but where he emerges will be left to the decision of the storyteller if he does not.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits + Streetwise</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Action: </b>Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">The demon has successfully accessed the Hallway, but at a part of it that is dangerous to the demon in some way. This may be because angels are using nearby doors or because nearby doors in the Hallway all lead to an inconvenient location. Roll for compromise.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Failure: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">The embed fails to function and the door does not change.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Success: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">The demon has successfully accessed The Hallway, and may use it to escape the area. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>Exceptional Success: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">The demon has successfully accessed the Hallway, right where he needs to, and the door directly across the hall from the entrance he used to enter will lead to his desired destination. This means the demon does not need to use the embed a second time in order to get to where he wants to go.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\"><b>The Hallway (Sidebar Style!)</b></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">The Hallway is a quantum space similar to a demon's bolthole. The origins of the Hallway are unknown, but the God-Machine's angels (and even sometimes its especially favoured agents) utilise it to move unseen from place to place or to influence the world at a moment's notice.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">Aesthetically the Hallway appears to be a never-ending hallway with evenly spaced doors on either wall. The decoration and trappings of the Hallway are never the same on any visit. Sometimes it can appear to be a long, up-scale Art Deco hotel hallway, with each door being a room. While on another occasion it could be a long hospital hallway on a ward, where each door should lead to a patient's ward.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">However some things are always the same about the Hallway. The doors are never numbered or labelled in a way that makes sense to the human mind. The numbers may be impossibly large or incomprehensible, causing eye-strain and headaches when peered at, or they may be absent entirely. Every door looks the same and each repeated feature is identical \u2013 right down to chips, stains and aging on the decorations.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri, sans-serif\">The Hallway, although it can be accessed by demons, is a God-Machine construct and as such any demon using it runs the risk of being noticed by the God-Machine and it's servants. Demons regard the Hallway with caution, for they don't really know why or where it exists; some even speculate that it may be the access-hub of Heaven itself.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 06-21-2014, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T09:52:19-07:00","id":176088,"title":"","content":"Leetespeak, I have to thank you for your necromancy. I had forgotten about this thread and in my mind thought that backdoor was in the actual book! I would have been sad if none of my players had seen it because it wasn't there. I've added your version to the list of embeds for my players.<br /> <br /> And I love the random, story -driving potential of your dramatic failure. I think it helps counter balance the Primum miles being too good issue that was discussed before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T05:23:57-07:00","id":178818,"title":"","content":"Gotta say, love this embed. Combined with a bolt hole with easy access and you've got one extremely hard to pin down demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T06:47:50-07:00","id":184764,"title":"","content":"I'm glad to see renewed interest in this and the variety of ways people people have come up with to implement it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here's a version I've been toying with, based on the idea of limiting the Embed by forcing the Demon to designate destinations beforehand, but also freeing it from any range limitation:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shortcut:</b><br /> Use any door you can open to get to any door you have 'tagged.' Can have [Primum] tagged doors at once.Tag a new door by touching it and focusing for an Instant action.<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits + Streetwise<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Success:</b> The Demon travels travels through a door he can open, arriving through any of the doors he currently has tagged.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheFrigidMidget</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9785-building-an-embed?p=178818#post178818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta say, love this embed. Combined with a bolt hole with easy access and you've got one extremely hard to pin down demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Demon I built this Embed for is planned to have an Easy-Access Bolthole, the Four Minutes Ago Exploit, and Teleportation and Mirror Skin as part of his Demonic Form. If you can lock him up something's gone very, very wrong.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9785-building-an-embed?p=176088#post176088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leetespeak, I have to thank you for your necromancy. I had forgotten about this thread and in my mind thought that backdoor was in the actual book! I would have been sad if none of my players had seen it because it wasn't there. I've added your version to the list of embeds for my players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh WOW I feel pretty prideful that someone misremembered this Embed as something official <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":478,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","user":"Intrepid Vector","date":". 06-30-2014, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T08:27:46-07:00","id":184847,"title":"","content":"I like that version a lot, Intrepid. Since Backdoor is terminology used in <i>Flowers of Hell</i>, your use of Shortcut helps the Embed stand out. I think your version has the least moving parts so to speak, and that's for the best. Some more description would be awesomely cool. Does a Demon have to touch a door to designate it a Shortcut, or can they do it when they see it?<br /> <br /> I think my only criticisms are that I'd love to see your ideas for a Dramatic Failure or an Exceptional Success, and that I think the Demon should be able to reflexively untag doors to facilitate a quick escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T09:18:29-07:00","id":184883,"title":"","content":"I really like your Dramatic Failure so I may use that if you don't mind, or something similar, and will work on attaching full fluff to this one. The Demon has to touch the door to use it, yes. Not sure what you mean about untagging for a quick escape?<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T10:11:33-07:00","id":184926,"title":"","content":"I mean if I've tagged the door to my Safe Place and I'm running through Oscorp's 3rd Floor, if I tag the closet to quickly let me escape from the security guards pursuing me, reflexive untagging would allow me to untag it after I go through, meaning those security guards will pour into the supply closet instead of my Safe Place, wondering where the hell I went.<br /> <br /> For the fluff, I'd refer to my version or to that Exploit that lets you quantum entangle two different spaces. In fact, your version with the tagging would make a great prerequisite for that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T10:17:54-07:00","id":184930,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay. That's something I could see you doing simply shutting the door behind you to end the Embed. In my most recent version, you don't 'tag' the door you enter, you're just making it, for the brief period it's open, lead to one of your 'tagged' doors. I think I explained that badly. PenDragon had a version on Page 1 where you add both the entry and exit doors to your tagged doors, but in this version, the tagged doors just functions as exits, with entry doors being &quot;This door I'm touching when I activate the Embed&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sorry if this is incoherent, I'm about to head to bed :T","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T10:21:09-07:00","id":184933,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay, sounds good.<br /> <br /> Have a good night!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T10:43:09-07:00","id":186411,"title":"","content":"Okay, I built up my version of the Embed, with a generous handful of advice and editing from Satchel:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <b>\u200bShortcut:</b><br /> A closed door is a portal full of unresolved potential, liable to take you anywhere. While it's reasonable to assume what's on the other side (&quot;My closet.&quot; &quot;The break room.&quot;), the connections between discrete locations are more flexible than they seem. A Demon who knows how to take advantage of this uncertainty can substitute one location behind a door for another, if just for the moment it takes them to pass through.<br /> <br /> A Demon lays the groundwork for this power by touching a door and concentrating as an Instant action. This door is now 'tagged' by the character, standing out among the countless other portals that separate places from each other. The Demon can have up to [Primum] tagged doors at once, each one remaining tagged for roughly a month after the character sets them. From any point after this they can activate this Embed while opening a door\u2014any door\u2014to have it lead through one of their tagged doors instead of where it logically should.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Wits + Streetwise<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b>\u200b The door is misconnected, accessing a 'utility corridor' used by agents of the God-Machine instead of the Demon's intended destination. These not-quite-places are backdoors used by angels, cryptids, and other strange creations of the God-Machine, none of whom are likely to take well to an unscheduled encounter.<br /> <b>Failure: </b>The door opens to where it normally would, but the character can try to use the Embed again.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The Demon opens a door, connecting it to any of the doors she currently has tagged, ignoring crude things like 'distance' and 'spatial geometry.' The door remains open for [successes] minutes unless it is closed earlier by hand.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The door can remain open for up to a scene or hour. Using the door is a reflexive action. Should the demon find himself ambushed on the other side, he adds his Primum to the roll to react to surprise as well as his Initiative</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}